<title>CANADA: Seagram closes sale of Putnam Berkley.</title>
<headline>Seagram closes sale of Putnam Berkley.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Seagram Co Ltd said on Tuesday that it completed the sale of its publishing division, The Putnam Berkley Group, Inc., to the Penguin books unit of Pearson Plc.</p>
<p>The transaction closed following early termination of the Hart Scott Rodino waiting period, Seagram said.</p>
<p>The sale of Putnam by Seagram's 80-percent-owned entertainment unit MCA Inc for US$336 million was announced on November 26.</p>
<p>Putnam Berkley is a leading U.S. publisher of popular fiction.</p>
<p>((Reuters Montreal bureau 514-985-2434))</p>
</text>
